// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: expects 1 argument, got 3
// BUG-860: spawn had no arity check at all — the per-argument loop is bounded
// by the PARAM count, so extras were silently dropped and only GCC complained
// ("too many arguments to function"), with no source line. The direct call
// `worker(1,2,3)` was already rejected: two spellings of one program.
void worker(u32 v) { }
u32 main() { spawn worker(1, 2, 3); return 0; }
